      "writtenOn": "2019-04-23T02:16:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "getSubscriptionProperty is null/garbage-safe anyway. We shouldn\u0027t assume here that everything is going to be happy just because the subscriptionId is \u003e -1. It\u0027s possible to have a valid subId that refers to nothing or to a valid subId that doesn\u0027t have a valid integer in the DB. I think a 2-step check should be used:\n1) check for null\n2) call Integer.valueOf() and catch NumberFormatException.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3581,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 3581,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "2bf41642e14dd7f43f83cd126e08f89b7f7a0dc8",
